{"units": [{"id": "patrios-note1", "translation": "[πατρίᾳ [fatherland] M for πατρώᾳ [paternal].]"}, {"id": "patrios-quote1", "translation": "the ancestral drink of Scamander"}, {"id": "patrios-word1", "translation": "fatherland"}, {"id": "patrios-word2", "translation": "paternal"}, {"id": "patris-orth1", "translation": "fatherland"}, {"id": "patris-def1", "translation": "fatherland."}, {"id": "patris-note1", "translation": "in elegy"}, {"id": "patris-quote1", "translation": "and the fatherland, the earth"}, {"id": "patris-quote2", "translation": "free the fatherland"}, {"id": "patris-quote3", "translation": "defending the fatherland"}, {"id": "patrothen-orth1", "translation": "from the father, on the father's side"}, {"id": "patrothen-def1", "translation": "from the father, on the father's side."}, {"id": "patrothen-note1", "translation": "See Lobeck, Pathologiae Elementa vol. 2 p. 246."}, {"id": "patrothen-quote1", "translation": "nor did the auspicious utterance from the father fail"}, {"id": "patrothen-quote2", "translation": "and from the father an avenger would become a helper"}, {"id": "patroktones-orth1", "translation": "to kill one's father"}, {"id": "patroktones-def1", "translation": "to kill one's father."}, {"id": "patroktones-quote1", "translation": "For will you, who killed your father, live with me?"}, {"id": "patroktonos-orth1", "translation": "father-killing, parricide"}, {"id": "patroktonos-def1", "translation": "killing one's father, parricide."}, {"id": "patroktonos-quote1", "translation": "Oedipus the father-killer"}, {"id": "patroktonos-quote2", "translation": "and father-killers, destroyers of houses"}, {"id": "patroktonos-quote3", "translation": "and addressing this father-killing web"}, {"id": "patroktonos-quote4", "translation": "father-killing pollution"}, {"id": "patrosteres-orth1", "translation": "deprived of one's father"}, {"id": "patrosteres-def1", "translation": "deprived of one's father."}, {"id": "patrosteres-quote1", "translation": "offspring deprived of their father"}, {"id": "patrophonos-orth1", "translation": "father-killer"}, {"id": "patrophonos-def1", "translation": "killer of one's father."}, {"id": "patrophonos-quote1", "translation": "with father-killing hand"}, {"id": "patronymios-orth1", "translation": "taking one's name from one's father"}, {"id": "patronymios-def1", "translation": "taking one's name from one's father."}, {"id": "patronymios-note1", "translation": "Scholium: \"ὅτι κατὰ πατέρα συγγενὴς ἡμῖν, τουτέστιν ὁ ἐκ προγόνων ἰθαγενής [that he is related to us through his father, that is, the native-born from our ancestors].\" With the form of the adjective are to be compared the compounds ἐπωνύμιος [named after] and παρωνύμιος [derived from a name]."}, {"id": "patronymios-quote1", "translation": "How then fares King Xerxes, born of Darius, the patronymic race of ours?"}, {"id": "patronymios-word1", "translation": "that he is related to us through his father, that is, the native-born from our ancestors"}, {"id": "patronymios-word2", "translation": "named after"}, {"id": "patronymios-word3", "translation": "derived from a name"}, {"id": "patroios-orth1", "translation": "paternal, ancestral"}, {"id": "patroios-def1", "translation": "paternal."}, {"id": "patroios-def2", "translation": "It is a surname of certain gods, especially those whom the Greeks worshipped as founders and protectors of their race: on which see Thesaurus vol. 6 p. 619."}, {"id": "patroios-def3", "translation": "ancestral."}, {"id": "patroios-note1", "translation": "Thus Heath for πατρίᾳ [fatherland]."}, {"id": "patroios-quote1", "translation": "you hear the dishonored ancestral woes"}, {"id": "patroios-quote2", "translation": "scarcely persuading the ancestral mind"}, {"id": "patroios-quote3", "translation": "he sat on the ancestral throne"}, {"id": "patroios-quote4", "translation": "he will hold the city and the care of the ancestral house"}, {"id": "patroios-quote5", "translation": "dividers of ancestral wealth"}, {"id": "patroios-quote6", "translation": "having taken the ancestral homes"}, {"id": "patroios-quote7", "translation": "and not to increase ancestral wealth"}, {"id": "patroios-quote8", "translation": "defiling ancestral hands with maiden-slaughtering streams"}, {"id": "patroios-quote9", "translation": "and ancestral prayers and omens"}, {"id": "patroios-quote10", "translation": "he mowed down the ancestral house"}, {"id": "patroios-quote11", "translation": "paying for the devices of the ancestral hand"}, {"id": "patroios-quote12", "translation": "Hermes of the underworld, watching over ancestral powers"}, {"id": "patroios-quote13", "translation": "and overseers of ancestral eyes"}, {"id": "patroios-quote14", "translation": "ancestral hunt"}, {"id": "patroios-quote15", "translation": "being accomplished from ancestral blood"}, {"id": "patroios-quote16", "translation": "from ancestral homes"}, {"id": "patroios-quote17", "translation": "and he dwells in ancestral wealth"}, {"id": "patroios-quote18", "translation": "revering the ancestral fate"}, {"id": "patroios-quote19", "translation": "altar of Zeus the ancestral"}, {"id": "patroios-quote20", "translation": "pollution of the ancestral gods"}, {"id": "patroios-quote21", "translation": "and seats of the ancestral gods"}, {"id": "patroios-quote22", "translation": "the ancestral city"}, {"id": "patroios-quote23", "translation": "he calls upon the gods of his race, of the ancestral land"}, {"id": "patroios-quote24", "translation": "nor in the misery of the ancestral land"}, {"id": "patroios-quote25", "translation": "allotments of ancestral tombs"}, {"id": "patroios-quote26", "translation": "and being holy in ancestral rites"}, {"id": "patroios-quote27", "translation": "wretched in his race and in his ancestral land"}, {"id": "patroios-quote28", "translation": "the ancestral soil of the Argive land"}, {"id": "patroios-quote29", "translation": "love of this ancestral land"}, {"id": "patroios-quote30", "translation": "and instead of the ancestral altar the block awaits"}, {"id": "patroios-quote31", "translation": "to stain the ancestral ground with blood"}, {"id": "patroios-quote32", "translation": "for from ancestral homes they brought a slavish fate"}, {"id": "patroios-quote33", "translation": "deprived of the ancestral land"}, {"id": "patroios-quote34", "translation": "ancestral homes"}, {"id": "patroios-quote35", "translation": "with ancestral laurel-bearing ox-sacrificing honors"}, {"id": "patroios-word1", "translation": "fatherland"}, {"id": "pauroi-orth1", "translation": "few"}, {"id": "pauroi-def1", "translation": "few."}, {"id": "pauroi-quote1", "translation": "few indeed out of many"}, {"id": "pauroi-quote2", "translation": "for to few men is this akin"}, {"id": "pausanemos-orth1", "translation": "stilling the wind"}, {"id": "pausanemos-def1", "translation": "putting an end to the storm."}, {"id": "pausanemos-note1", "translation": "second syllable long"}, {"id": "pausanemos-quote1", "translation": "sacrifices to the wind-stiller"}, {"id": "pauo-orth1", "translation": "to make cease, to stop"}, {"id": "pauo-def1", "translation": "to make cease or desist, to put an end to."}, {"id": "pauo-def2", "translation": "Passive"}, {"id": "pauo-def3", "translation": "to cease."}, {"id": "pauo-def4", "translation": "With the genitive."}, {"id": "pauo-def5", "translation": "With the participle."}, {"id": "pauo-note1", "translation": "in a corrupt passage"}, {"id": "pauo-quote1", "translation": "I stopped mortals from foreseeing their doom"}, {"id": "pauo-quote2", "translation": "nor did Zeus himself stop the upright from bringing back the dead"}, {"id": "pauo-quote3", "translation": "stop the water in the manner of fire"}, {"id": "pauo-quote4", "translation": "and the hatred has ceased"}, {"id": "pauo-quote5", "translation": "and by unharmed strength and divine inspirations violence is stopped"}, {"id": "pauo-quote6", "translation": "and to cease from a humane disposition"}]}